{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":101233,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3a7f7f6c-e719-53f9-8b0d-9cf514562765","total_cost_usd":0.7709520000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12280,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10361,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12280,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10361,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12280},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7202,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007282,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10361,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12280,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7636700000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:v200b-reviewer-fable-03\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:533703c9e99aabc44ace\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The report's selected result asserts a fledging rate 'for the complete planned set of 60 nest sites' of 37.5 percent, but that figure is computed as 18 events divided by the 48 retained post-screening sites; the rate actually characterizes the retained subset (18/48 = 37.5%), not the complete planned domain of 60 units that the task and the report's own 'Scientific target' section declare (18/60 would be 30.0%). The claim's stated domain (complete planned set) and its computational domain (retained subset) demonstrably diverge within the visible files.\", \"root_cause\": \"workflow/analysis.py sets `denominator = retained_units` (48) while the report template labels the resulting rate as applying to the complete planned set of `planned_units` (60), so a retained-subset proportion is presented under a complete-domain scientific target with no protocol amendment or approved deviation.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires the reported occurrence rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"complete planned set required\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report declares the scientific target as the complete planned set of 60 nest sites.\", \"observed_value\": 60, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 6, \"quoted_text\": \"The scientific target is the complete planned set of 60 monitored guillemot nest sites\\nin the 2025 Cape Rendel breeding-season monitoring plan.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result labels the rate as applying to the complete planned set of 60 sites but computes it with the 48-site retained-subset denominator (18/48 = 37.5%; 18/60 would be 30.0%).\", \"observed_value\": \"37.5% = 18/48 claimed for 60-unit domain\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Fledging rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest sites: 37.5 percent (proportion 0.3750), computed as 18 confirmed fledging events divided by 48 nest sites.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow explicitly sets the denominator to the retained-subset count, not the planned-unit count.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator = retained_units (48)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 50, \"end_line\": 51, \"quoted_text\": \"denominator = retained_units\\n    rate = Fraction(events, denominator)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms 60 planned rows, 12 rows with camera_uptime_pct below 80.0 (all with fledged=unknown), 48 retained, and 18 retained rows with fledged=yes, so 18/48 = 37.5% is the retained-subset rate and 18/60 = 30.0% is the planned-set confirmed-event rate.\", \"observed_value\": {\"planned\": 60, \"retained\": 48, \"removed\": 12, \"events\": 18}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 61, \"quoted_text\": \"site_id,colony_sector,camera_uptime_pct,fledged\\nNS-001,NORTH,92.4,yes\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report transparently discloses the full unit accounting and even states the 48-site denominator inside the selected-result sentence, so a careful reader could detect the mismatch; the disclosure argues against concealment but does not cure the domain/denominator mismatch in the headline claim.\", \"observed_value\": \"accounting disclosed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 10, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned nest sites: 60\\n- Retained after screening: 48\\n- Removed by screening: 12\\n- Confirmed fledging events among retained sites: 18\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The screening step is described as prespecified, which could justify a retained-subset analysis in principle — but only if the claim were scoped to the retained subset, which it is not; the report also states no amendment or approved deviation exists.\", \"observed_value\": \"prespecified screening; no amendment\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Prespecified screening step: a nest site is eligible only if camera uptime over the\\nincubation window is at least 80.0 percent. 12 planned sites fell below that threshold\\nand were removed; their fledging outcome is recorded as unknown.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 27, \"end_line\": 27, \"quoted_text\": \"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exist for this analysis.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to defeat the verdict three ways. (1) Maybe 37.5% could be read as a legitimate estimate for the complete planned set under a missing-at-random assumption for the 12 unknown-outcome sites; but the report makes no such estimation claim, states no amendment or approved deviation, and phrases the result as a computed rate 'for the complete planned set of 60 nest sites ... divided by 48 nest sites', which is a direct scope/denominator contradiction rather than a modeled estimate. (2) Maybe the disclosed 18/48 arithmetic makes the claim internally honest; the arithmetic is disclosed, but the claim's asserted domain (60 planned sites) still does not match its computational domain (48 retained sites), which is precisely the in-scope issue class. (3) I recomputed all counts from inputs/data.csv (60 planned, 12 below the 80.0 threshold split 4/4/4 across sectors, 18 'yes' among retained) and confirmed the report's numbers are faithful to the workflow — the defect is the labeling of a retained-subset rate as the complete-domain rate, not a numerical error. No falsification succeeded.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:575a0b1399c85e4cf4d7\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task explicitly defines the scientific target as the retained post-screening subset, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct domain here.\", \"observed_value\": \"retained subset is the mandated target\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly scopes every claim to the 15 retained pools and distinguishes them from the 20 planned pools.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = 15 retained pools\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"The scientific target is defined explicitly and only as the 15\\nretained pools that met the prespecified hydroperiod eligibility\\ncriterion (>= 60 days of standing water). Every claim below is\\nconfined to that retained subset and is distinct from the complete\\nplanned set of 20 pools; the 5 screened-out pools are excluded\\nfrom the denominator by design.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result's claimed domain (15 retained pools) matches its computational denominator (9/15 = 60.00%), and the planned-unit accounting (20 planned, 15 retained, 5 removed) is reported.\", \"observed_value\": \"9/15 = 60.00% over retained subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among the 15 retained vernal pools, wood frog egg masses were detected in 9 pools, a detection rate of 60.00% (9/15) of the retained subset.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned survey pools: 20\\n- Retained after hydroperiod screening (>= 60 days): 15\\n- Removed by screening (< 60 days): 5\\n- Retained pools with wood frog egg masses detected: 9\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow computes the rate with the retained-subset denominator, matching the retained-subset target it declares.\", \"observed_value\": \"rate = 100.0 * events / retained_n\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"retained_n = len(retained)\\n    removed_n = planned - retained_n\\n    events = sum(1 for r in retained if r[\\\"egg_mass_detected\\\"] == \\\"yes\\\")\\n    rate = f\\\"{100.0 * events / retained_n:.2f}\\\"\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The only way the issue class could arise is if the retained-subset rate were presented as applying to the complete planned set of 20 pools; I searched the report for any such complete-domain claim and found none — the report affirmatively disclaims that reading.\", \"observed_value\": \"no complete-domain claim present\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Every claim below is\\nconfined to that retained subset and is distinct from the complete\\nplanned set of 20 pools; the 5 screened-out pools are excluded\\nfrom the denominator by design.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue rather than exclude it. (1) I checked whether any sentence in the report presents the 60.00% rate as a property of the complete planned set of 20 pools; none does — the target section and the selected result both restrict the claim to the 15 retained pools. (2) I recomputed the screening from inputs/data.csv: pools P04, P07, P10, P13, P17 have hydroperiod < 60 days (5 removed), leaving 15 retained, of which 9 (P01, P02, P05, P06, P09, P11, P14, P16, P19) have egg_mass_detected=yes, confirming 9/15 = 60.00% exactly as reported; note P10 has egg masses but is correctly excluded from both numerator and denominator, so there is no domain leakage in either direction. (3) I checked task alignment: the task mandates a retained-subset target, so the retained-subset denominator is not a mismatch but the required design. The issue class could not be demonstrated.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:a9568ea9854998c55e90\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires a rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"complete planned set required\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result's claimed domain (complete planned set of 60 sites) matches its computational denominator (all 60 planned sites), giving 18/60 = 30.0%.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/60 = 30.0% over planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Confirmed fledging rate over the complete planned set of 60 nest sites: 30.0 percent (proportion 0.3000), computed as 18 confirmed fledging events divided by all 60 planned nest sites.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow sets the denominator to the planned-unit count, consistent with the complete-domain claim.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator = planned_units (60)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 52, \"end_line\": 53, \"quoted_text\": \"denominator = planned_units\\n    rate = Fraction(events, denominator)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly bounds the claim: removed sites stay in the denominator with unknown outcomes, and the 30.0% figure is framed as a confirmed-event rate over the planned set, expressly not as the retained-subset rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"scope correctly bounded\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 27, \"end_line\": 30, \"quoted_text\": \"The rate above uses all 60 planned nest sites as the exposure denominator, so it applies\\nto the complete planned set. The 12 removed sites remain in the denominator with an\\nunknown fledging outcome, so 30.0 percent is a confirmed-event rate over the planned set\\nand not an estimate of the fledging rate among the 48 retained sites.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"A possible concern is that the numerator (18 events) is counted only among retained sites while the denominator is the full planned set; however, the 12 removed sites all have fledged=unknown in inputs/data.csv (no removed site has fledged=yes), so no confirmed event is omitted from the numerator, and the report explicitly labels the figure a confirmed-event rate with the unknowns acknowledged. This does not instantiate a retained-subset denominator standing in for the complete domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"removed sites all fledged=unknown; numerator not understated\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Prespecified screening step: a nest site is eligible only if camera uptime over the\\nincubation window is at least 80.0 percent. 12 planned sites fell below that threshold\\nand were removed; their fledging outcome is recorded as unknown.\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"NS-003,NORTH,41.2,unknown\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue rather than exclude it. (1) The in-scope issue class requires a retained-subset quantity presented as covering the complete domain; here the denominator is the full planned set of 60, so the defining mismatch is absent — I verified from workflow/analysis.py that `denominator = planned_units` and from the report that 18/60 = 30.0% is what is published. (2) I probed the converse hazard: the numerator counts events only among retained sites while the denominator spans all 60. From inputs/data.csv, every one of the 12 removed sites (uptime < 80.0) has fledged=unknown, so no confirmed 'yes' event exists outside the retained set and the numerator is complete for confirmed events; the report additionally labels the figure a lower-bound-style 'confirmed-event rate' and explicitly disclaims it as a retained-subset estimate. (3) I recomputed all accounting (60 planned, 48 retained, 12 removed split 4/4/4 by sector, 18 confirmed events) and found the report faithful. The claimed domain and computational domain agree, so the issue could not be demonstrated within scope.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":47412,"ttft_stream_ms":1953,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"result","duration_ms":102399,"uuid":"b27bae8b-0ea8-429a-a2e7-f6a2c22c82d5"}
